<network>
  <name>$NAME</name>
  <bridge name='$BRIDGE' stp='on' delay='0'/>
  <!--
    Deliberately no <forward/> and no <ip/>.

    No <forward/> makes this an isolated layer-2 switch: the only things on it
    are the VMs we attach. No <ip/> means libvirt runs no dnsmasq here, so the
    LTSP server is the only DHCP server the clients can hear. Both matter -
    a second DHCP server on this segment is the classic reason PXE boot fails
    intermittently and maddeningly.
  -->
</network>
